From: thongass000 <tienthong2004@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 5 Nov 2026 10:50:00 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 18/18] imsservice: Report camera capabilities in sensor
 orientation

AOSP's dialer treats CameraCapabilities as sensor-orientation dimensions:
VideoCallFragment.updatePreviewVideoScaling() swaps them before handing
them to VideoScale, because it expects a landscape frame. Samsung reports
the portrait pair instead, so the preview came out zoomed 1.78x
((1/0.75) * (1080/2220) * 2.74) with most of the frame cropped away.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 ...oCallProviderImpl$ImsVideoCallEventListener.smali | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/smali/com/google/ims/ImsVideoCallProviderImpl$ImsVideoCallEventListener.smali b/smali/com/google/ims/ImsVideoCallProviderImpl$ImsVideoCallEventListener.smali
index d45a50e..72a7d35 100644
--- a/smali/com/google/ims/ImsVideoCallProviderImpl$ImsVideoCallEventListener.smali
+++ b/smali/com/google/ims/ImsVideoCallProviderImpl$ImsVideoCallEventListener.smali
@@ -334,7 +334,7 @@
     :cond_2
     new-instance v0, Landroid/telecom/VideoProfile$CameraCapabilities;
 
-    invoke-direct {v0, p2, p3}, Landroid/telecom/VideoProfile$CameraCapabilities;-><init>(II)V
+    invoke-direct {v0, p3, p2}, Landroid/telecom/VideoProfile$CameraCapabilities;-><init>(II)V
 
     .line 861
     .local v0, "cameraCapabilities":Landroid/telecom/VideoProfile$CameraCapabilities;
